# SCRIPT: 10_UI__Set_Hub_Tab
# FOLDER: 10_UI
# ROLE: switch the hub's active tab. Thin on purpose.
# CALLED BY: hub tab buttons ; 30_CONTEXT__Select_Property_Context ; 70_SCHEDULE__Generate_Expected_Schedule
# CALLS: nothing
# INPUTS: $p (JSON) — { "tab":<req>, "subtab":<opt> }
# GLOBALS IN: none
# RETURNS: { ok, tab } | { ok:false, error }
# GLOBALS OUT: g_HubTab, optionally g_HubSubTab
# SIDE EFFECTS: none beyond globals + a window refresh. Writes NO business data.
#
# 🥇 STATE: GOLDEN. The 2026-06-18 audit called it "current enough" and it is the only
#   script that survived that pass unscathed — because it does exactly one thing.
#
# THE RULE THAT KEEPS IT USEFUL:
#   NO heavy data mutation here. Ever. The moment a tab switch starts posting records or
#   generating schedules, every button on the hub becomes unpredictable and you can no
#   longer reason about what a click costs. Tab switching is display state.
#   If a tab needs data prepared, the CALLER prepares it and then calls this.
#
# WHY IT VALIDATES THE TAB NAME:
#   A typo'd tab name would otherwise set a global to garbage and leave the hub on a blank
#   panel with no error — the layout object just fails to match. Failing loudly on an
#   unknown tab is cheaper than debugging an empty screen.
#
# CHANGELOG:
#   - 2026-06-18 audited, kept as-is.
#   - 2026-07-29 ported from ClickUp into a real per-script body; tab-name validation added
#     because a silent blank panel is the failure mode this script would otherwise have.

# --- SETUP ---
Set Error Capture [ On ]
Set Variable [ $p ; Value: Get ( ScriptParameter ) ]
Set Variable [ $tab ; Value: JSONGetElement ( $p ; "tab" ) ]
Set Variable [ $subtab ; Value: JSONGetElement ( $p ; "subtab" ) ]

If [ IsEmpty ( $tab ) ]
	Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; False ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "error" ; "no tab" ; JSONString ] ) ]
End If

# --- VALIDATE against the known panel set. Keep this list in sync with the hub layout. ---
Set Variable [ $known ; Value: "Summary¶Schedule¶Ledger¶Receipts¶Payoff¶Documents" ]

If [ not PatternCount ( $known ; $tab ) ]
	Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; False ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "error" ; "unknown tab: " & $tab ; JSONString ] ) ]
End If

# --- SET DISPLAY STATE ---
Set Field [ GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES::g_HubTab ; $tab ]

If [ not IsEmpty ( $subtab ) ]
	Set Field [ GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES::g_HubSubTab ; $subtab ]
End If

Refresh Window [ ]

Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; True ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "tab" ; $tab ; JSONString ] ) ]
